Third-party notices

EUP is MIT (../LICENSE). The two Mac programs, the installer program (which every
installer made with EUP is a copy of) and EUP, the packager application, also contain
code from these projects; their notices go with them:

  newlib.txt                 newlib, the C library (BSD-style notices)
  multiversal.txt            Multiversal Interfaces (MIT)
  retro68-gcc-runtime.txt    Retro68's runtime and GCC's libgcc (GPL v3 or later
                             with the GCC Runtime Library Exception)
  inflate.txt                Mill's gzip decoder, in the installer program (MIT)

Nothing under the GPL alone, or the LGPL, is in either program. The command-line
packager, eup, is EUP's own code and the C library of the system it's built on.
On the release disk, these notices are the "Licenses" file.
